# Deploy (API and SPA)

Single guide: `docs/deployment/hostinger.md`.

- Two Hostinger Node sites on Cloud Startup, both on the `migration/backend-api` branch (for now, owner 2026-10-26): API (root `apps/api`, entry `dist/main.js`) and SPA (root `apps/web`, output `dist`, entry `serve-dist.mjs`). Build command **empty** on both: the host cannot run `vite build` (native esbuild, `noexec`).
- `.github/workflows/release.yml` merges `release` into `migration/backend-api` and commits `apps/*/dist` and one `pnpm-lock.yaml` per app in the same commit. Never commit build output to other branches (PLAT-06) and never push to `migration/backend-api` by hand.
- Cut a release: `git checkout release && git merge --ff-only mvp && git push origin release`.
- Database: one SQL file from `node apps/api/scripts/build-hostinger-sql.mjs` (`--users` for the importable file with users, gitignored). Never `prisma db seed` on the host. Never a VPS, never a second MySQL.
- Env only in hPanel (`DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `CORS_ORIGIN`, `UPLOAD_DIR` outside the site folder, `WEB_LEADS_KEY`); the SPA's API URL is baked from `apps/web/.env.production`.
